      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d2b5d0b_e9c6f86e",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-22T17:09:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not? It is convoluted, but i2c/spi based EC can, using MKBP event.\nFor LPC, mkbp events are sent through host events. See https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DZd1jwXt6O_oDUxg__rTJ_tCf4zsGBYzkel2JU4ULCA/edit?tab\u003dt.0",
      "parentUuid": "dab0f50e_2c92afc5",
      "revId": "621f9c7db5bc377df50afe84c0f373633690ef8d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af31597c_f7c16abd",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-22T17:15:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what the technical limitation is, but when we tried it over the HECI bus it would crash the ISH and we would need to cold reboot the device to recover. We can loop Intel back into this to ask.",
      "parentUuid": "4d2b5d0b_e9c6f86e",
      "revId": "621f9c7db5bc377df50afe84c0f373633690ef8d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae872d4e_68439771",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4141,
